1
00:00:00,099 --> 00:00:01,919
Public toilet seats have a gap at the front,

2
00:00:02,139 --> 00:00:03,519
and the one in your house almost certainly

3
00:00:03,579 --> 00:00:04,179
does not.

4
00:00:04,219 --> 00:00:04,939
It is written down.

5
00:00:05,219 --> 00:00:06,960
The plumbing codes most of the country builds

6
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,159
to call for open-front seats in public restrooms,

7
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,839
and have for over fifty years.

8
00:00:11,119 --> 00:00:12,859
The gap keeps the seat clear of the area

9
00:00:12,939 --> 00:00:14,599
you are most likely to touch while wiping,

10
00:00:14,799 --> 00:00:16,899
which matters far more when hundreds of strangers

11
00:00:16,979 --> 00:00:17,719
share one seat.

12
00:00:17,959 --> 00:00:19,539
It also leaves urine nowhere to pool.

13
00:00:19,819 --> 00:00:21,539
What reads as cost-cutting is a rule.
